WEBVTT

00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:26.193
Well, what'll it be, folks?
Tap water or bottled?

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:28.362
Whatever. Kif, you pick.

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:31.406
Oh. Oh, it's always so hard to decide.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.325
Um, tap. I mean, bottled.

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:36.537
Bam.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.840
Ooh, I love your boots, Leela.

00:00:39.923 --> 00:00:41.967
Nobody would ever guess they're knockoffs.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.136
- How could you tell?
- I guessed.

00:00:44.219 --> 00:00:46.388
They're at it again.

00:00:46.471 --> 00:00:47.639
Please, Fry.

00:00:47.723 --> 00:00:49.933
Girlfriends always talk trash
to each other.

00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:54.021
Like, how I might say I like Amy's dress
'cause it covers all her tramp stamps.

00:00:55.272 --> 00:00:56.732
Knock it off, Fry.

00:00:56.815 --> 00:01:00.110
It's when women are polite to each other
that you know there's a problem.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.528
Exactly.

00:01:01.612 --> 00:01:04.615
Now, enough about who is
and who isn't a Chinese skank.

00:01:04.698 --> 00:01:07.200
We're just two happy couples
on a double date.

00:01:17.336 --> 00:01:18.754
Let's go. Let's go.

00:01:18.837 --> 00:01:22.174
We've got to get these moon rocks
to the moon by moondown.

00:01:22.257 --> 00:01:25.719
Why are we bringing moon rocks
to the moon?

00:01:25.802 --> 00:01:28.055
Oh, those lunar crybabies claim

00:01:28.138 --> 00:01:31.016
the rocks were stolen
by the Apollo astronauts.

00:01:31.099 --> 00:01:34.144
They consider them part
of their cultural heritage.

00:01:37.231 --> 00:01:39.983
Nice work, Leela.
You're really pulling your weight.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.401
Which is saying something.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.571
Ow!

00:01:52.037 --> 00:01:53.997
You're using the rocks
to build a wall?

00:01:54.081 --> 00:01:56.124
What about your cultural heritage?

00:01:56.208 --> 00:01:59.294
You bought that cultural heritage hoo-ha?

00:01:59.378 --> 00:02:02.005
What a bunch of big-city dummies.

00:02:02.089 --> 00:02:03.757
At least the rocks are light here.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:06.426
I don't even need
my over-the-shoulder boulder holder.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:09.888
With one-sixth gravity, you can work
and be lazy at the same time.

00:02:09.972 --> 00:02:11.557
It's like being a voice actor.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.142
Say, you nose-breathers want to come see

00:02:14.226 --> 00:02:16.019
some real moon culture,

00:02:16.103 --> 00:02:18.647
come on down
to the Butterfly Derby tonight.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.149
Wait, the Butterfly Derby is when?

00:02:21.233 --> 00:02:22.234
And what?

00:02:32.828 --> 00:02:36.623
The low gravity lets them nice ladies
flap every which way,

00:02:36.999 --> 00:02:40.460
so long as they only wear light,
skimpy outfits.

00:02:40.544 --> 00:02:42.921
It's a necessity of the sport, it is.

00:02:43.005 --> 00:02:46.550
This is actually quite elegant.
It's not what I was expecting.

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:49.011
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:02:49.094 --> 00:02:52.264
please welcome the meanest things
on gossamer wings...

00:02:52.347 --> 00:02:54.266
The Murderflies.

00:02:58.687 --> 00:03:00.564
This is what I was expecting.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:03.108
So, uh, what are the rules of this sport?

00:03:03.191 --> 00:03:04.359
You see that there?

00:03:04.443 --> 00:03:06.028
That's called a floor.

00:03:06.111 --> 00:03:08.822
Once a butterfly hits that, she's out.

00:03:08.906 --> 00:03:10.991
Last team flying wins.

00:03:11.074 --> 00:03:13.452
Super Swatter!

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:20.667
Yeah. Yay, yay, yay.

00:03:28.008 --> 00:03:31.553
Keep your eye on the ground.
That's where she's going to land.

00:03:32.429 --> 00:03:34.389
Yep, called it.

00:03:36.099 --> 00:03:39.353
And now, for our weekly
amateur flapdown.

00:03:39.436 --> 00:03:42.856
Do we have two volunteers
to go wing-to-wing with the Murderflies?

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:46.360
Winners get 50 bucks and the accolades
of dozens of hooting hillbillies.

00:03:49.238 --> 00:03:50.614
What do you think, Leela?

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:54.284
Judging from your tank top,
you love getting hooted at by hillbillies.

00:03:54.368 --> 00:03:58.455
And you could use the $50
for another gallon of Hello Kitty perfume.

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.749
The bicker sisters teaming up?

00:04:00.832 --> 00:04:03.001
Talk about cat women on the moon.

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:08.548
Okay, enough of that already.
We're not really fighting.

00:04:08.632 --> 00:04:10.717
Then prove it. By fighting.

00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:13.345
All right, we will. Come on, Amy.

00:04:15.138 --> 00:04:17.891
Why don't you and I
ever do things together?

00:04:24.481 --> 00:04:25.732
This is hard.

00:04:25.816 --> 00:04:28.569
Now I know why butterflies
are always so grouchy.

00:04:28.652 --> 00:04:31.196
Please welcome
tonight's volunteer victims,

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.366
Turanga Leela and Amy Wong.

00:04:34.449 --> 00:04:36.618
Hang on.
We're not quite ready to...

00:04:40.622 --> 00:04:43.083
You girls have moxie.

00:04:43.166 --> 00:04:44.751
We're gonna beat it out of you.

00:04:44.835 --> 00:04:47.588
Amy, remember when
we tried out for the Rockettes?

00:04:47.671 --> 00:04:50.924
And we failed because we accidentally
kicked those two Rockettes to death?

00:04:51.008 --> 00:04:52.676
Yeah. Why do you bring that up?

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.511
Oh.

00:05:02.519 --> 00:05:05.564
We'll teach you not to lose immediately.

00:05:08.025 --> 00:05:10.152
Super Shocker.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.141
Yay! They can move their arms.

00:05:41.225 --> 00:05:45.395
Congratulations to our gutsy,
non-paralyzed challengers.

00:05:47.189 --> 00:05:50.776
Ladies, that is the kind
of can-do performance I like to see...

00:05:50.859 --> 00:05:52.986
From my new Butterfly Derby team.

00:05:53.237 --> 00:05:55.364
Which is what I'm offering you to be.

00:05:55.447 --> 00:05:57.824
Because I'm the commissioner
of the Butterfly Derby.

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:00.118
I'm Abner Doubledeal. Hello.

00:06:00.202 --> 00:06:01.495
But we lost.

00:06:01.578 --> 00:06:03.288
Why would you want us to join your league?

00:06:03.372 --> 00:06:06.291
We're always looking for fresh blood,
and you girls are full of it.

00:06:06.375 --> 00:06:07.751
You two could be the next big thing.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.503
What happened to the last big thing?

00:06:09.586 --> 00:06:11.588
Nothing that doesn't happen
to everyone eventually.

00:06:11.672 --> 00:06:13.173
What is this, an inquisition?
You in or not?

00:06:14.174 --> 00:06:16.218
- Yes.
- You spletcha.

00:06:17.135 --> 00:06:20.389
And so began the fight career
of two skimpy outfits

00:06:20.472 --> 00:06:22.432
and the feisty women who filled them.

00:06:22.516 --> 00:06:24.810
Ladies and gentlemen, the WingNuts.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:28.397
And although
sometimes they got beaten,

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.400
other times, they got beaten badly.

00:06:32.568 --> 00:06:35.279
But just when it looked
like they'd never win...

00:06:36.321 --> 00:06:37.531
They didn't.

00:06:37.781 --> 00:06:40.158
Well, we lost to all our opponents.

00:06:40.242 --> 00:06:42.953
Even that team that turned out
to be us in the mirror.

00:06:43.036 --> 00:06:44.121
It's time we gave up.

00:06:44.204 --> 00:06:46.081
Yeah. I don't know what else

00:06:46.164 --> 00:06:48.458
we could have done
to enhance our performance.

00:06:48.542 --> 00:06:50.752
Hey, great job tonight, you two.

00:06:50.836 --> 00:06:52.546
Here, got you some fresh Nectar.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:58.010
Whoa, that puts the lead in my pencil.

00:06:58.093 --> 00:06:59.678
Thanks, trainer.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:03.891
Excuse me.

00:07:03.974 --> 00:07:05.601
What's that nectar you're handing out?

00:07:05.684 --> 00:07:09.187
It's a plant-based supplement
that bulks up your flapping muscles.

00:07:09.271 --> 00:07:11.481
Want to try it? You know you want to.

00:07:11.565 --> 00:07:14.985
A chemical that can help us win?
That sounds great.

00:07:15.277 --> 00:07:17.779
Mmm, I'm not sure.

00:07:17.863 --> 00:07:20.282
Look, here's my disposable
cell phone number.

00:07:20.365 --> 00:07:22.284
Think it over.
Give me a call when you're...

00:07:22.367 --> 00:07:24.661
Hang on. I got to take this. Hello?

00:07:24.745 --> 00:07:26.079
- We're ready.
- Great.

00:07:26.914 --> 00:07:28.665
You are not gonna regret this.

00:07:28.749 --> 00:07:31.293
It's a nice, clean way
to improve your performance.

00:07:31.376 --> 00:07:32.419
And we just drink it?

00:07:32.502 --> 00:07:33.503
Or...

00:07:33.587 --> 00:07:36.214
Inject it between your toes.
Either way works, right?

00:07:38.717 --> 00:07:40.969
Well, down the hatch.

00:07:43.847 --> 00:07:46.266
Mmm. A guy could get used to this.

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:54.149
Once again, Eternulax The Immortal,

00:07:54.233 --> 00:07:56.235
dead at the age of 26.

00:07:57.861 --> 00:08:00.280
Now here's Sportsbot 5000 to tell us

00:08:00.364 --> 00:08:03.325
about two local gals,
Amy Wong and Turanga Leela,

00:08:03.408 --> 00:08:06.411
who have won 15
Butterfly Derby bouts in a row,

00:08:06.495 --> 00:08:08.914
even as rumors swirl
that they're juicing up

00:08:08.997 --> 00:08:11.250
with the controversial
nutritional supplement

00:08:11.333 --> 00:08:13.543
known as Nectar. Sportsbot?

00:08:14.044 --> 00:08:15.587
That's pretty much it.

00:08:15.671 --> 00:08:17.923
Riveting stuff, Sportsbot.

00:08:18.006 --> 00:08:20.175
- Yo, yo, yo.
- What's up, ladies?

00:08:23.804 --> 00:08:25.681
Uh-oh, the bullies are back.

00:08:25.764 --> 00:08:29.101
Leela, Amy, I like a stalwart,
feminine physique

00:08:29.184 --> 00:08:30.936
as much as the next fellow,

00:08:31.019 --> 00:08:33.105
but this Nectar worries me.

00:08:33.188 --> 00:08:35.023
You should be worried about this.

00:08:35.107 --> 00:08:36.233
Boo-ya!

00:08:36.316 --> 00:08:37.901
Easy, Amy, easy.

00:08:37.985 --> 00:08:39.987
Professor, there's nothing
wrong with Nectar.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:41.196
It's all-natural.

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:46.118
So are carrots, but you don't see me
injecting them between my toes.

00:08:54.001 --> 00:08:56.211
Uh, Leela?

00:08:56.295 --> 00:08:58.547
I was wondering if you'd like
to go out with me again.

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:01.425
Maybe play some miniature golf
or colossal tennis?

00:09:01.508 --> 00:09:02.509
Sorry, Fry.

00:09:02.593 --> 00:09:05.512
I already got a double date
with arm and hammer.

00:09:07.472 --> 00:09:09.558
Bender, you want to go out
and do something?

00:09:09.641 --> 00:09:13.437
Oh, so, now I'm your
last-resort booty call, huh?

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:14.688
Okay, let's go.

00:09:32.664 --> 00:09:34.541
That's my little sugar doodle.

00:09:34.625 --> 00:09:36.752
Cork your face bladder. I'm working.

00:09:36.835 --> 00:09:38.921
Sorry. I had that coming.

00:09:39.004 --> 00:09:41.048
It's not easy being a derby wife.

00:09:41.506 --> 00:09:43.592
The WingNuts, ladies and gentlemen,

00:09:43.675 --> 00:09:46.178
and that bloodbath takes them
to next week's finals

00:09:46.261 --> 00:09:49.431
against our reigning champions,
the Murderflies.

00:09:53.018 --> 00:09:54.144
Now, listen up.

00:09:54.228 --> 00:09:56.647
I got a little boy at home,
and he's dying.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.233
Dying to see me kill these two.

00:10:01.151 --> 00:10:03.403
Oh, your son's gonna die, all right,

00:10:03.487 --> 00:10:04.571
but from neglect.

00:10:04.655 --> 00:10:07.574
'Cause you're going home in an urn.

00:10:07.658 --> 00:10:09.576
A funerary urn.

00:10:14.081 --> 00:10:16.250
Hey, trainer, we got a big bout next week.

00:10:16.333 --> 00:10:19.253
- Juice us up.
- Sorry, gals, I'm all out.

00:10:19.336 --> 00:10:21.546
These two just bought my entire supply.

00:10:23.674 --> 00:10:25.551
You're going...

00:10:26.385 --> 00:10:27.678
Down.

00:10:31.557 --> 00:10:33.976
And she doesn't even want
to cuddle anymore.

00:10:34.059 --> 00:10:36.687
She just wants to hit me
with various chairs.

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:40.482
You're lucky. I can't even get Leela
to verbally abuse me.

00:10:41.358 --> 00:10:42.651
All right, listen up.

00:10:42.734 --> 00:10:45.320
We're out of Nectar,
and we need a new source.

00:10:45.404 --> 00:10:49.700
Uh, dearest, perhaps this would be
a good time to consider possibly drinking

00:10:49.783 --> 00:10:51.493
just a little less...

00:10:51.577 --> 00:10:54.746
Say, why don't you just have Kif
get you some Nectar?

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:57.416
It comes from a flower on his home planet.

00:10:57.499 --> 00:10:59.876
You mean it's ocephalus nectar?

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:01.795
Oh, my. Oh, dear.

00:11:01.878 --> 00:11:03.755
It's found in a rather remote region...

00:11:03.839 --> 00:11:06.592
Just play along.
This could be our chance for romance.

00:11:06.675 --> 00:11:09.887
Uh, come on, ladies.
Let's take a little trip to Kif's planet.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:13.181
We'll gather some nectar
and have a nice, romantic weekend.

00:11:13.265 --> 00:11:14.641
Just the four of us.

00:11:14.725 --> 00:11:17.519
Let's go already!

00:11:35.746 --> 00:11:39.666
Wow. It's the second most
beautiful thing I've ever seen.

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.920
Hey, Leela, want to know what
the most beautiful thing is?

00:11:43.003 --> 00:11:44.755
No. Let's get hopped up.

00:11:47.758 --> 00:11:49.885
Greetings, eco-tourists.

00:11:49.968 --> 00:11:53.889
I am the grand butterfly curator...
This week.

00:11:53.972 --> 00:11:56.600
Yeah, yeah, you can teach us
to respect nature later.

00:11:56.683 --> 00:11:58.977
Right now, we've got
some flowers to suck dry.

00:11:59.061 --> 00:12:00.979
Suck 'em, burn 'em,
as long as they're not butterflies,

00:12:01.063 --> 00:12:02.648
I don't give a grand crap.

00:12:03.023 --> 00:12:04.441
But take heed,

00:12:04.524 --> 00:12:06.818
for you see, it is mating season.

00:12:07.569 --> 00:12:11.406
Whatever you do,
you must not disturb the aggressive male.

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:14.201
He can be identified
by his orange coloration

00:12:14.284 --> 00:12:16.370
and enormous butterjunk.

00:12:16.453 --> 00:12:19.039
What's he gonna do,
migrate at us?

00:12:20.207 --> 00:12:21.291
Silence.

00:12:21.375 --> 00:12:25.087
I can't be specific about the danger,
since if something different happens,

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.922
I might be liable for damages.

00:12:27.005 --> 00:12:28.548
But believe me,

00:12:28.632 --> 00:12:31.343
you'll rue the day you came

00:12:31.426 --> 00:12:33.637
to the Butterfly Preserve.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:35.681
Well, enjoy the Butterfly Preserve.

00:12:35.764 --> 00:12:38.058
Okay, bye. Come on, come on.

00:12:38.141 --> 00:12:40.811
Let's find those flowers.
We'll split into teams.

00:12:40.894 --> 00:12:42.312
You mean couples?

00:12:42.396 --> 00:12:44.064
Eh? Eh?

00:12:45.232 --> 00:12:46.775
Nice job smacking Kif.

00:12:46.858 --> 00:12:48.235
Dude had it coming. Wait.

00:12:48.318 --> 00:12:50.445
I think I smell Nectar.

00:12:50.529 --> 00:12:52.531
Way ahead of you.

00:12:56.285 --> 00:12:57.911
I don't even know why we're helping find

00:12:57.995 --> 00:13:00.998
an addictive drug
for our mean girlfriends.

00:13:01.081 --> 00:13:02.791
Quiet, they'll hear you.

00:13:06.378 --> 00:13:08.839
The male butterfly. It's gorgeous.

00:13:08.922 --> 00:13:11.592
- Let me get my butterfly hammer.
- Bender, no.

00:13:11.675 --> 00:13:14.845
That park ranger explicitly
gave us a vague warning.

00:13:14.928 --> 00:13:17.389
Look, the hammer's already out,
I got to smash something.

00:13:35.908 --> 00:13:38.410
It smells like a skunk

00:13:38.493 --> 00:13:40.329
stuffed with feta cheese.

00:13:40.412 --> 00:13:42.372
P.U...

00:13:42.456 --> 00:13:44.499
Thank God I don't have a nose.

00:13:48.337 --> 00:13:50.422
We can sleep at my parents' house.

00:13:50.505 --> 00:13:52.674
I'll just buzz
and let them know we're here.

00:13:55.636 --> 00:13:58.597
Mom, Dad, I'm sure you remember

00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:00.390
Fry, Leela, Bender,

00:14:00.474 --> 00:14:03.101
and of course, my Fonfon Ru, Amy.

00:14:03.185 --> 00:14:05.437
Welcome to our home.

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:07.105
One of you stinks.

00:14:07.189 --> 00:14:09.775
That'd be me. Wait, you're flies.

00:14:09.858 --> 00:14:11.109
Don't you eat excrement?

00:14:11.193 --> 00:14:13.820
That's a day at the beach
compared to this.

00:14:13.904 --> 00:14:17.282
Listen, I'm just gonna shower
this stuff off and go to bed.

00:14:17.366 --> 00:14:19.451
Wait. Don't take a shower, Fry.

00:14:19.534 --> 00:14:21.328
You smell kinda nice.

00:14:21.411 --> 00:14:23.205
Sm...

00:14:23.288 --> 00:14:24.456
Yeah. Huh?

00:14:24.539 --> 00:14:26.250
No hanky-panky.

00:14:26.333 --> 00:14:29.127
Everyone sleep in separate rooms.

00:14:29.211 --> 00:14:30.837
Good night, Kif.

00:14:30.921 --> 00:14:32.673
- Night, Fry.
- Huh?

00:14:36.385 --> 00:14:38.136
Keep your door unlocked tonight.

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:40.097
But McGruff the Crime Dog says...

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:41.807
Oh.

00:14:55.904 --> 00:14:57.906
Come in!

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:09.543
Hey, smelly-pants.

00:15:09.626 --> 00:15:11.545
- Leela.
- Leela?

00:15:11.628 --> 00:15:13.380
- Amy?
- Amy.

00:15:13.463 --> 00:15:16.508
I'm done polishing my ass, Fry.
Here's your toothbrush back.

00:15:27.269 --> 00:15:29.938
You just hop into bed with my boyfriend?

00:15:30.022 --> 00:15:34.026
And you. As God is my witness,
I'll never forgive you for this.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:40.198
Hey, just 'cause he's your boyfriend
doesn't mean you get him all to yourself.

00:15:41.992 --> 00:15:44.077
He's mine.
There's nothing more to talk about.

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:46.246
No, no, keep talking.

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:48.123
Um, Amy, I hope I'm not

00:15:48.206 --> 00:15:49.875
- out of line, but...
- Shut up, Kif.

00:15:49.958 --> 00:15:52.461
How dare you talk that way to my Kif?

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:57.257
This planet's got it going on.

00:16:00.302 --> 00:16:03.472
Sweet orgy of Georgia.
Have you girls gone wild?

00:16:03.555 --> 00:16:05.182
That's Fry you're macking on.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:11.813
Hmm. It seems Fry's
inexplicable sex appeal

00:16:11.897 --> 00:16:15.192
is due to the butterfly pheromone
he was sprayed with.

00:16:15.275 --> 00:16:18.570
But Amy and Leela
aren't butterflies. Right?

00:16:18.654 --> 00:16:21.615
No, but thanks to
the damned butterfly nectar

00:16:21.698 --> 00:16:24.076
they've been swilling,
they might as well be.

00:16:26.078 --> 00:16:28.288
The nectar causes their bodies to produce

00:16:28.372 --> 00:16:30.332
female butterfly hormones,

00:16:30.415 --> 00:16:32.251
building up their flapping muscles,

00:16:32.334 --> 00:16:33.335
but also making them

00:16:33.418 --> 00:16:36.672
irresistibly attracted to Fry.

00:16:36.755 --> 00:16:39.091
The only way to end this madness

00:16:39.174 --> 00:16:42.427
- is for the ladies to quit, cold turkey.
- Whoa, whoa.

00:16:42.511 --> 00:16:44.346
Let's not shock their system.

00:16:44.429 --> 00:16:46.723
Maybe they could just go warm turkey?

00:16:46.807 --> 00:16:48.517
No, the Professor's right.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:50.143
We have to quit the Nectar.

00:16:50.227 --> 00:16:52.646
I agree. This has to stop.

00:16:55.899 --> 00:16:57.693
Oh...

00:16:57.776 --> 00:16:59.611
My guts feel kinda weird.

00:16:59.695 --> 00:17:00.946
I'm not surprised.

00:17:01.029 --> 00:17:03.699
Those pheromones were highly concentrated.

00:17:03.782 --> 00:17:07.786
Oh, I think I'm getting
a little caterpilly.

00:17:17.963 --> 00:17:20.674
All right, let's get this party ended.

00:17:36.565 --> 00:17:38.650
We did it. We kicked Nectar's butt.

00:17:38.734 --> 00:17:41.028
I don't give a crap.

00:17:41.111 --> 00:17:45.616
Kif, I'm sorry for
making out with Fry so loud and often.

00:17:45.699 --> 00:17:49.661
It's all right, dearest.
I know it was just the Nectar talking

00:17:49.745 --> 00:17:51.079
and groping.

00:17:51.163 --> 00:17:55.500
Well, looks like Fry's three-way
is down to a one-way. If he's lucky.

00:17:55.584 --> 00:17:57.711
Hey, where is Fry?

00:18:04.968 --> 00:18:06.553
Amy, Leela, what are you doing

00:18:06.637 --> 00:18:08.430
at your place of work?
Your match with the Murderflies

00:18:08.513 --> 00:18:10.474
is about to start.

00:18:15.854 --> 00:18:17.439
Moon-ladies and moon-men,

00:18:17.522 --> 00:18:19.566
presenting the defending champions,

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:23.028
the queens of hostility
from the Sea of Tranquility,

00:18:23.111 --> 00:18:24.821
the Murderflies.

00:18:28.909 --> 00:18:31.703
And now their opponents,
the vixens most horrible

00:18:31.787 --> 00:18:33.372
from the big blue marble,

00:18:33.455 --> 00:18:34.873
the WingNuts.

00:18:36.375 --> 00:18:38.710
Everybody kill everybody.

00:18:38.794 --> 00:18:40.879
Well, we're not on the juice anymore,

00:18:40.963 --> 00:18:42.714
but what's the worst that can happen?

00:18:42.798 --> 00:18:45.092
Since this is a championship match,

00:18:45.175 --> 00:18:47.261
we are gonna need some lava.

00:18:49.096 --> 00:18:51.390
Wait. Hot lava?

00:18:53.934 --> 00:18:56.019
Amy, if we get killed, I just wanna say

00:18:56.103 --> 00:18:58.397
it's been an honor riding
the roller coaster of addiction

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:02.276
and recovery with you, as a team.

00:19:13.787 --> 00:19:15.455
How could this not be hurting you?

00:19:15.539 --> 00:19:17.749
I once killed a sea turtle
with these boots.

00:19:19.501 --> 00:19:21.837
Hold me.

00:19:46.904 --> 00:19:48.488
Oh, no. Oh, no. Oh, no, no.

00:19:48.572 --> 00:19:50.115
- Oh, no.
- Make a wish.

00:19:59.875 --> 00:20:01.043
My God.

00:20:01.126 --> 00:20:04.755
Fry has metamorphosed
into a gigantic butterfly.

00:20:04.838 --> 00:20:07.424
He's even more beautiful than before.

00:20:12.262 --> 00:20:15.057
Oh, what is that sexy stink?

00:20:17.517 --> 00:20:20.437
Oh, cripes. They're mating.

00:20:21.813 --> 00:20:23.273
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:20:23.357 --> 00:20:26.360
I am so sorry
for allowing this lurid sex act

00:20:26.443 --> 00:20:29.863
to taint an otherwise delightful day
of family-friendly violence.

00:20:31.573 --> 00:20:34.910
That is some freaky bug-on-bug action.

00:20:34.993 --> 00:20:36.787
I feel a little left out.

00:20:42.542 --> 00:20:45.337
- Is Fry gonna be okay?
- I don't think so.

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:48.090
He's grown all these strange insect parts,

00:20:48.173 --> 00:20:51.009
and he has absolutely no brain activity.

00:20:52.511 --> 00:20:55.180
Look, he lost the strange insect parts.

00:20:58.433 --> 00:20:59.768
He's back to normal.